{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793019266,"nonce":"C4TDmC0YgHuB1R8HoFDIicX7X20=","title":"Scope browser recovery to verified workspace and account identities","message":"Remaining browser-session isolation slice from 080ea85416efa648d8a634f8a1906bdecb0e70bf9da9cf934675d832d8533081 and 670bd15d5f2a4c8fdd82da62e9b72599f9a689affc5682a7b621f81fd72156c0.\n\nSessionClient currently names IndexedDB document recovery and the full editor's private workspace metadata from socket origin/path plus hello.name. Reusing an endpoint for another same-named workspace can merge old local CRDT edits into the replacement. Hosted compute replacement also needs an authority-owned stable identity, independent of guest filesystem paths or temporary VM addresses.\n\nImplement persistent opaque local authority/workspace IDs, verified account scope, gateway-owned identity on hosted handshakes, unambiguous versioned browser cache keys, and a reconnect fence before any old document can sync into a different context. Legacy unscoped caches must not be loaded automatically. Preserve same-workspace offline recovery and authorized anonymous-to-signed-in draft handling. Report a changed context to the full editor, retain the old recovery cache and require explicit reopening.\n\nValidate same endpoint/display-name replacement, same-workspace restart, different accounts, hosted compute identity changes and normal multi-client CRDT behavior. Rebuild/stage WASM and session and restart local services at the checkpoint. Keep DO document authority, MSB provisioning and aggregate quotas open.","files":null}]}